message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during this admission. You're here because your left arm dialysis access isn’t working—it’s clotted again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I couldn’t get dialysis yesterday. My arm felt cold and numb. Is it fixable this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to try. You’ve had this graft for a while, and it’s had multiple clots. The last imaging showed a problem with the artery feeding it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan? Another surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re scheduling you for a procedure tomorrow morning—left arm exploration. We’ll see if we can open the clot and fix the blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if you can’t fix it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use your tunneled catheter in your neck for dialysis. It’s already in place, so we can use it right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I just want to get back on track with dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2118-08-10 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get you there. For now, we’ll run some blood tests and monitor your heart, given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Your hemoglobin is low, but stable. Kidney numbers are as expected for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been anemic for years. Is that still from my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s part of your end-stage renal disease. We’re not giving any transfusions now, but your team will manage it long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve also been nauseous—can’t keep pills down sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I saw that. You tried the long-acting nitrate and vomited. We’re switching you to a smaller, short-acting one three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2118-08-10 15:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That might help. The big pill always made me sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2118-08-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re going to surgery in an hour. The goal is to fix the graft, but we might find that it can’t be saved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2118-08-11 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. Just do what’s safest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. The surgery didn’t go as hoped. We opened the area, but the artery feeding the graft is too small and already past the split."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So you couldn’t fix it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. The blood flow wouldn’t be strong enough. We decided not to create a new connection. Your graft is no longer usable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll be on the neck catheter for good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. You have a follow-up with your access surgeon to discuss options—maybe a new graft in your right arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a lot. But as long as I can keep dialysis, I’ll manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll get you dialyzed today. The catheter was sluggish, so we’ll use TPA to clear it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "TPA? Isn’t that for strokes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2118-08-11 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same medication, but here we use a small dose inside the catheter to dissolve clots. It’s safe and common."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your dialysis session completed. We couldn’t remove fluid because your blood pressure dropped, but the treatment worked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt dizzy. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with your heart history. We’ll adjust your settings at the outpatient unit to go slower."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my chest X-ray—was it okay? I had some shortness of breath after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the X-ray showed your lungs are clear. No pneumonia or fluid. Your heart is large, but that’s chronic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2118-08-11 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2118-08-11 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you another dose of TPA in the catheter overnight to keep it open. We’ll flush it out tomorrow before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2118-08-11 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that affect my bleeding risk?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2118-08-11 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Minimal risk—it’s only in the catheter, not your bloodstream. We’re watching closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We removed the TPA from your catheter. Your incision is healing well—no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’m going to rehab today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to the extended care facility for 30 days. You’ll keep going to outpatient dialysis three times a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your gynecologist will contact you about the ultrasound. You have a heart and access clinic follow-up scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—the ultrasound showed fibroids and something about the lining?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the endometrium was slightly thick. They’ll want to check it more closely, but it’s not urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my meds—are they the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mostly. The long-acting nitrate is replaced with a smaller pill three times a day. You can crush it in applesauce if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’ll help. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember—no blood pressure checks or blood draws on your left arm. Keep the incision dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no heavy lifting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Nothing over 10 pounds. Call the access clinic if your hand turns blue, cold, or numb."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. The rehab team will help you transition. We’ll keep coordinating with your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2118-08-12 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Let’s get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave—your vitals are stable, and you’re alert and walking well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Nervous, but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. You’ve been through a lot. The rehab team knows your plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And dialysis starts tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, at your usual center. They’re expecting you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll see them then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes before your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2118-08-12 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2118-08-10 13:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2118-08-12 12:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a thrombosed left upper extremity AV graft, which prevented dialysis access. She underwent surgical exploration, but the procedure was aborted due to inadequate arterial inflow, making revision unfeasible. The graft was deemed non-salvageable, and hemodialysis was resumed using a tunneled catheter in the left internal jugular vein, requiring TPA to restore function. The patient tolerated dialysis with episodes of hypotension, and her incision healed without complications. Medication adjustments were made for nausea and hypotension, switching from long-acting to short-acting nitrates. A transvaginal ultrasound revealed a thickened endometrium and calcified fibroids, prompting planned gynecologic follow-up. She was discharged to a 30-day respite care facility with ongoing outpatient dialysis and scheduled appointments for vascular access and gynecologic evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerosis of autologous vein bypass graft of the extremities",
      "Anemia in chronic kidney disease",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Late effects of cerebrovascular disease, hemiplegia affecting nondominant side",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Long-term (current) use of other medications",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease"
    ]
  }
}
